[01:54:58.202] Browser LOG     [Interviewer] Question data: {"agentTemplateId":null,"aiCustomPrompt":null,"aiHelperName":null,"aiPromptTemplate":"helpful","category":"algorithm","createdAt":"2026-01-11T12:11:16.977818","currentStep":5,"deactivated":false,"deactivatedAt":null,"description":"Build a log aggregator that can write, read, and count log entries.\nLevels: \"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARN\", \"ERROR\"\n\nExample:\n  Logger logger = new Logger();\n \n  // Write logs (timestamp is auto-generated)\n  logger.write(\"INFO\", \"Server started\");      // t=1000\n  logger.write(\"ERROR\", \"Connection failed\");  // t=1001\n  logger.write(\"INFO\", \"Operation started\");   // t=1002\n  \n  // Read with filter (newest first)\n  LogFilter filter = new LogFilter();\n  filter.level = \"INFO\";\n  List<LogEntry> logs = logger.read(filter);\n  // Returns: [\n  //   {timestamp: 1002, level: \"INFO\", message: \"Operation started\"},\n  //   {timestamp: 1000, level: \"INFO\", message: \"Server started\"}\n  // ]\n  \n  // Count in time range\n  int count = logger.count(\"ERROR\", 1000, 1002);  // Returns: 1","difficulty":"medium","followUpQuestions":null,"followupQuestionsJson":"[{\"id\":\"fq_1768128343480_1zggckm\",\"question\":\"Walk me through the time complexity of your read() and count() methods\",\"expectedAnswer\":\"1. inMemory: \\n          \\\"approach\\\": \\\"Store all logs in List, filter in code\\\",\\n          \\\"readComplexity\\\": \\\"O(n) - scan all logs, filter matches\\\",\\n          \\\"countComplexity\\\": \\\"O(n) - scan all logs, count matches\\\"\\n2. memory with Level Index: \\n          \\\"approach\\\": \\\"Separate list per level: Map<String, List<LogEntry>>\\\",\\n          \\\"readComplexity\\\": \\\"O(k) - where k is logs with that level\\\",\\n          \\\"countComplexity\\\": \\\"O(k) - only scan relevant level\\\"\\n3.fileBased: \\n          \\\"approach\\\": \\\"Separate file per level or time period\\\",\\n          \\\"readComplexity\\\": \\\"O(m) - where m is bytes to read from disk\\\",\\n          \\\"countComplexity\\\": \\\"Same, but with I/O overhead\\\"\\n4.database: \\n          \\\"approach\\\": \\\"Indexed database with WHERE clauses\\\",\\n          \\\"readComplexity\\\": \\\"O(log n) with index - near instant\\\",\\n          \\\"countComplexity\\\": \\\"O(log n) - uses COUNT(*) with index\\\"\"},{\"id\":\"fq_1768128469022_97mujxu\",\"question\":\"How would you optimise count() if we only care about total counts (not time-filtered)?\",\"expectedAnswer\":\"Cache counts that don't depend on time filtering. Keep running totals that update on write()\"},{\"id\":\"fq_1768128549105_li3e30m\",\"question\":\"If multiple threads call write() at the same time, what happens? if needed- give me a solution to the problem \",\"expectedAnswer\":\"1. File-based, in-memory, or NoSQL database:\\nData can become corrupted when multiple threads write simultaneously. The solution is to have all writes go to a queue, where a single writer thread processes them sequentially.\\n2. SQL database:\\nSQL databases handle thread safety automatically through built-in locking mechanisms.\"},{\"id\":\"fq_1768129437734_qh5rxv7\",\"question\":\"If you have 10 microservices, how do you aggregate their logs into one place?\",\"expectedAnswer\":\"Each service still has its own logger. Logs are written to a standard output (or local file) in a consistent format.\\nA collector picks up the logs, adds metadata like service name / instance / environment / requestId, and ships them to a central store.\"}]","generatedLanguagesJson":"{\"java\":{\"generated\":false,\"reviewed\":true},\"python\":{\"generated\":true,\"reviewed\":true},\"javascript\":{\"generated\":true,\"reviewed\":true}}","id":293,"initialCodeJava":"class Logger {\n    public Logger() {\n        // TODO: implement\n    }\n    \n    public void write(String level, String message) {\n        // TODO: implement\n    }\n    \n    public List<LogEntry> read(LogFilter